# TestFlow architecture boundaries

QA E2E testing platform. Next.js frontend, FastAPI backend, separate Playwright runner,
Supabase persistence. Full design in `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/adr/`. Read `CLAUDE.md` before
non-trivial work.

These six rules are not negotiable. Each one has already been broken in this repo.

1. **FastAPI never launches a browser.** No `chromium.launch`, no `async_playwright()`, no
   subprocess that starts Playwright anywhere under `backend/`. The API creates a TestRun with
   status `queued`, enqueues `{ run_id }`, and returns. Browser work happens only in `worker/`.
2. **The runner executes the test it was asked to execute.** Resolve the requested test case and
   build the run from its stored definition. Never hardcode a path to a `.spec` file. If you
   find yourself writing a fixed filename, the design is wrong.
3. **Structured definitions are the source of truth.** Tests are stored as steps, locators and
   assertions. Never make a generated `.spec.js` file the thing that gets edited or replayed.
4. **Secrets are never plaintext.** Credentials and Playwright `storageState` are encrypted at
   rest and never appear in API responses, logs, exports, traces or fixtures.
5. **One entrypoint per service.** `backend/app/main.py` is the API. Do not add a second FastAPI
   app. Do not add code under `backend/src/` — that is dead NestJS from an unfinished migration
   and is pending deletion.
6. **One component per screen.** Do not create a second copy of a page component. This repo
   already has `src/views/X.tsx` and `src/views/<area>/X.tsx` pairs that drifted apart, and
   the routes load whichever was wired first. Edit the file the route imports.

## Scope discipline

Functional and Responsive testing only. Do not build AI test generation, self-healing selectors,
Firefox or WebKit, real devices, network or storage or accessibility capabilities, multi-tab
authoring, visual regression, load testing, scheduling, or native CI integrations. These are
designed in `docs/capability-roadmap.md` and deliberately deferred. Adding one is a scope change
the lead decides, not an implementation detail.

## Done means demonstrated

Work is done when it runs end to end and can be demoed. Code that compiles but is not wired to
the thing that calls it is not done, however complete it looks.
